Croquis is under the AGPL rather than the GPL for one specific reason: the GPL lets
someone host a modified Croquis as a service and never publish their changes. The AGPL's
section 13 closes that hole, and running it on your own machine costs you nothing.

It is AGPL-3.0 rather than something more permissive because it links simavr, which is
AGPL-3.0, and the two licences interlock by design. AGPL-3.0 section 13 grants permission
to link a GPL work with an AGPL one into a single combined work, with the AGPL's network
condition applying to the combination. So simavr remains GPL-3.0, and this work as a
whole is AGPL-3.0.


Bundled or linked third-party material
--------------------------------------

simavr — GPL-3.0
    The AVR instruction-level simulator the sketch actually runs on. Linked into
    the binary, and the reason the licence above is what it is.
    https://github.com/buserror/simavr

@wokwi/elements — MIT
    Draws the components: the Uno, the LED, the resistor, the pushbutton.
    https://github.com/wokwi/wokwi-elements

CodeMirror 6 — MIT
    The sketch editor.
    https://github.com/codemirror/dev

IBM Plex Mono and IBM Plex Sans — SIL Open Font License 1.1
    Bundled with the app rather than fetched from a font CDN, so that nothing here
    reaches the network.
    https://github.com/IBM/plex

Tauri — MIT or Apache-2.0
    The desktop shell.
    https://github.com/tauri-apps/tauri

Arduino AVR core 1.8.6 — LGPL-2.1
    Not shipped in this repository; obtained into .toolchain/ at build time and used
    by avr-gcc to compile your sketch. Your firmware therefore includes Arduino's
    core, under its own terms.
    https://github.com/arduino/ArduinoCore-avr


Not borrowed
------------

The breadboard is generated from a spec in src/lib/breadboard.ts rather than taken
from anywhere. The detailed third-party breadboard artwork that exists (Fritzing) is
CC-BY-SA, which cannot be baked into an AGPL-3.0 binary, so the drawing and the pin map
are built from one grid spec instead — which also means the two cannot drift apart.
